## 4. Contextual Bandits

A contextual bandit is a sequential decision-making framework that uses information about the current situation to select an action and learns from the resulting reward.

In dynamic pricing, the context describes the market situation, the action is the selected price, and the reward may represent profit.

### Core Concepts

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| Agent | The system making pricing decisions. |
| Environment | The market in which the agent operates. |
| Context | Information available before selecting a price. |
| Action | A pricing decision. |
| Reward | The outcome the agent seeks to maximize. |
| Policy | A rule or strategy for selecting actions. |
| Contextual Bandit | A decision-making framework that uses context to choose actions and learn from feedback. |
| Multi-Armed Bandit | A simpler bandit setting without contextual inputs. |
| Exploration | Trying actions to learn their outcomes. |
| Exploitation | Selecting an action believed to provide a high reward. |
| Exploration–Exploitation Trade-off | Balancing learning against immediate performance. |
| Cumulative Reward | The total reward obtained over multiple decisions. |
| Regret | The difference between achieved reward and an appropriate optimal benchmark. |
| Action Space | The set of available pricing actions. |
| Online Learning | Updating a model using newly observed data. |
| Offline Learning | Learning from an existing dataset. |
| Partial Feedback | Observing the outcome of the chosen action without observing every alternative. |

### Important Contextual Bandit Algorithms

| Algorithm | Main Idea |
|---|---|
| Epsilon-Greedy | Usually selects the best-known action but occasionally explores. |
| UCB | Uses an uncertainty-based bonus to guide exploration. |
| LinUCB | Uses a linear reward model and confidence bounds. |
| Thompson Sampling | Uses sampling from an estimated reward distribution to select actions. |
| NeuralUCB | Uses neural networks and uncertainty estimates for exploration. |
| NeuralTS | Uses neural reward modeling and sampling-based exploration. |

For this research, NeuralUCB and NeuralTS are potential candidates for the pricing decision component.

